MOA Val Package Assembly:
1.	Pick up Plan from the MOA Val Assembly Log by entering your name so others know it is being worked.
 
•	12/31/2021 MOA Plans located on this testing log assembly tab: MOA/Testing/2020 & 2021 Testing/2020 & 2021 MOA Testing Log.xlsx. 
 
•	12/31/2022 MOA Plans located on this testing log assembly tab: MOA/Testing/2023 Testing/ “MOA 2023Testing Log.xlsx.”
 
•	2022 MOA Off Calendar Plans located on this testing log assembly tab: MOA/Testing/2022 Testing/MOA 2022 Off Calendar Testing Log.xlsx.
 
•	2023 MOA Off Calendar Plans located on this testing log assembly tab: MOA/Testing/2023 Testing/ “MOA 2023 Off Calendar Testing Log.xlsx.”
 
 
2.	Go to the Plan’s Testing folder for the PYE being worked and find the “Valuation Package” folder and make sure all files in this folder are pdf, if any are not, then convert them to pdf or push back to the Tester and have them do it, so we reduce risk of Adobe crashing during the file combine process. (These should have been done already by the testing specialist)
 
•	The MOA Plan Folders are located at OmniBPO>(K:)/Mutual of America Folder/Plan Number
 
 
3.	Open Adobe and choose the “Tools” tab in upper left corner and then the “Combine Files” option
   
4.	Then hit the “Add Files” button to bring up the folder options:
 
 
 
5.	Go to the Plan’s Testing folder for the PYE being worked and find the “Valuation Package” folder and select all pdf files in that folder and hit “open”
 
6.	Using the Adobe Combine Tools, move the files in the correct order they need to be in and remove any files or pages not needed.
 
a.	The ordering of Reports/Misc. should be as follows:
 
1.	Cover Letter (Date on letter head should be single digit, i.e. 1 not 01)
2.	Test Summary
3.	Compensation Limit Failure Summary (for SHMa), if applicable
4.	Combined Testing Report, if applicable
5.	Action Required Page
6.	Failed Test Notice/Letter/Excess Summary, if applicable
7.	Variance Report(s), if applicable
8.	Year End Recap: Important Information
9.	Compliance and Administrative Reports: Overview and Descriptions
10.	Contribution Analysis
11.	HCE/Key (403b Plans should only indicate HCE)
12.	Future HCE
13.	ADP/ACP Tests, if only ADP Test should only indicate ADP Test, if only ACP Test should only indicate ACP Test.
Order below for ADP/ACP test pages if applicable
•	Summary Page (NOTE: some Plans may not have this page, this is ok, do not request)
•	ADP/ACP Test Detail
•	ADP/ACP Excluded
•	ADP/ACP Corrections Page
14.	402(g) Test
15.	410(b) Test
•	Detail report
•	Excludable report
•	Includable report
•	Summary report
16.	401(a)(4) Test, if applicable
17.	Average Benefit Percentage Test, if applicable (if component Plan may have more individual test which go in this order)
•	Average Benefit Percentage Test
•	401a1 Comp Test
•	Gateway Test, if applicable (may be part of the ABPT, if so leave with it)
•	Overall Comp test
•	Rate Group Comp Test
•	Sum Comp Test
18.	BRF Test (Benefits, Rights and Features test)
19.	414(s) Test, if applicable
20.	415 Limit Test
21.	Top Heavy
22.	Census
NOTE: MOA Plans will NOT have Statement Of Contribution Report but may have a Variance Report.
 
7.	Once files are in the proper order and unnecessary pages eliminated Click the Combine button in the upper right corner.
 
8.	If needed you can move individual pages around in the file after combining them using the thumbnail icon, located on the left of the Adobe screen.
 
9.	Save file as a PDF in OmniBPO/(K:)>Mutual of America>Plan number>Testing>YYYYTesting Folder as ######_2021-Valuation.pdf (###### = Plan Number)
 
a.	Final Valuation Package should be saved based on beginning of Plan year.
                                                              i.      i.e. 01/01/2017-12/31/2017 = YYYY = 2017
                                                            ii.      i.e. 02/01/2017-01/31/2018 = YYYY = 2017
                                                          iii.      i.e. 10/01/2017-09/30/2018 = YYYY = 2017
 
 
MOA 401(k) Editing/Review of Valuation Package:
NOTE: make sure “Mutual of America” is the ONLY entity mentioned in a MOA Valuation Package.
 
A.	COVER PAGE:
a.	Make sure you are working a MOA Plan. The upper right of the Cover Letter should show this Company stamp:
 
 
b.	Verify the Company Name, Company Address, Plan Name, and Plan Year End is pulling correctly for the Plan and PYE you are assembling.
 
 
B.   ACTION REQUIRED:
1. Leave the below paragragh if testing fails and returns are required (does not apply to ADP/ACP test or if failure does not cause a return) otherwise remove.
NOTE: do not include if 402g failure not processed by 4/15 deadline and this is noted on the 402(g) test
 
•	Make sure the wording looks like this:
 
 
 
 
 
 


 
 
2.  Leave the below paragraph if ADP/ACP Test failed using PRIOR method and Returns are required, otherwise remove.
- NOTE: if ADP Test is fixed using Reclassification or Shifting Methods, this paragraph is not needed, since returns would not be applicable
 
 
 
3.  Leave the below paragraph if ADP/ACP Test failed using CURRENT method and Returns are required, otherwise remove. (The difference between Current/ Prior failure wording is Current wording has the additional QNEC sentence in it,)
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
4. Leave the paragraph below if ADP/ACP Test fails using CURRENT method and being corrected after 12 months of the plan year end, otherwise remove.
 
5. Leave the paragraph below if ADP/ACP Test fails using PRIOR method and being corrected after 12 months of the plan year end, otherwise remove.
 
 
 
 
 
NOTE: MOA Plans will not use Escalation wording.        
 5. If Valuation Package has Variance Report or the Comment section of the Val Assembly Template states the below paragraph is needed, you will keep the following paragraph on the Annual Valuation Report/Action Required.
 
 6. Look at the Test Summary: If the Plan has a Top Heavy percent of 60% or over then you will need to keep this section, otherwise remove.
 
 
7.   If none of the Immediate Action Items listed above apply then only show the green line item below on the Annual Valuation Report/Action Required page.
 
 
 
 
NOTE: for the Compensation Limit Failure Summary there will be no special wording on the Action Required page on these.
 


C.)    ADP/ACP Failure Notice
1. If the Plan fails ADP/ACP testing using the CURRENT method ONLY and returns are required, then you  will include the following ADP/ACP Failure notice:
 
•	You will need to input the QNEC amounts on this CURRENT testing failure notice which will be found on the correction page of the ADP/ACP test.
 
“ADP/ACP test is $X,XXX,XXX.XX” = the total of both ADP QNEC and the ACP QNEC found on the correction page  (e.g. $142.540.41 + 42,814.34 = $185,354.75)
“ADP QNEC is” = ADP QNEC found on the correction page. (e.g., $142.541.41)
“ACP QNEC is” = ACP QNEC found on the correction page. (e.g., $42,814.34)
(This screen shot shows when both ADP and ACP Test fail) 
If only the ADP or ACP Test fails, then the correction page will look like this, so you will need to pay attention to what you are reading.
 
 
NOTE: If the ADP/ACP Test is not showing an ADP QNEC or ACP QNEC total then you will remove from the Failure notice on the one not represented on the ADP/ACP Correction Test Page.
 
NOTE: If the ADP/ACP Test using PRIOR method fails with returns we do NOT include this Failure notice in the Val Package.
2. If ADP/ACP Test fails using CURRENT method and is being corrected after 12 months of the plan year end, then you will include the following ADP/ACP Failure notice:
 
•	You will need to input the QNEC amounts & Refund amounts on this After 12 months testing failure notice which will be found on the correction page of the ADP/ACP test.
 
“ADP/ACP test is $X,XXX,XXX.XX” = the total of both ADP QNEC and the ACP QNEC found on the correction page. (e.g. $142.540.41 + 42,814.34 = $185,354.75)
“ADP QNEC is” = ADP QNEC found on the correction page. (e.g., $142.541.41)
“ACP QNEC is” = ACP QNEC found on the correction page. (e.g., $42,814.34)
(This screen shot shows when both ADP and ACP Test fail) 
If only the ADP or ACP Test fails, then the correction page will look like this, so you will need to pay attention to what you are reading.
 
“Deferral Contribution of $” total Deferral Refund amount. (e.g., 17,571.0) 
 
 
“Match Contribution of $” total Match refund amount. (e.g.,116.60)  
 
 
 
3. If ADP/ACP Test fails using PRIOR method and is being corrected after 12 months of the plan year end, then you will include the following ADP/ACP Failure notice:
 
•	You will need to input the Refund amounts on this After 12 months testing failure notice which will be found on the correction page of the ADP/ACP test.
“Deferral Contribution of $” total Deferral Refund amount. (e.g., 17,571.0) 
 
“Match Contribution of $” total Match refund amount. (e.g.,116.60)
 
D.) Annual Additions (IRC 415) Test Failure Information
 - Remove if Plan did not fail 415 (no 415 returns)
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
E. Sample Letter for ADP/ACP
- Remove if Plan did not have ADP/ACP
- Remove if Plan did not Fail or Failed and did not have returns required.
 
F. Sample Letter for failed 402(g)
- Remove if Plan did not have returns for 402(g)
 
NOTE, if 402g not processed prior to 4/15 deadline and this is noted on 402g report do not include the sample letter.
 
G. Sample Letter for failed 415 annual additions
- Remove if Plan did not fail 415 (no 415 returns)
 
H.  Excess Summary Report
- Normally you will only see an excess summary report for failures that are not ADP/ACP related, unless the ADP/ACP Failure is for a partially vested participant.
 
I. Year End Recap: “Important Information” Page:
 
•	Follow the notes on the below example on what bullet point to use and remove from the Important information page:
 
 
 
1.	Reading the ADP/ACP Test for PRIOR Testing bullet changes:
 
•	Determine which paragraph is applicable base on testing method type, no HCE or if Plan is SH. (If needed open the docinfo.xls file in the Plan’s Testing folder to determine)
 
•	 You can determine ADP/ACP Testing method by looking at the ADP/ACP test itself on the ADP/ACP Test Results page of the Valuation Package and look for the following wording to let you know if it is “Prior Testing” and if no wording then it is “Current Testing”
 
•	To calculate the Actual Deferral Percentage for the HCE’s on a “Prior Test”, look for the NHCE % on the ADP/ACP test.
 
 
