416 Top Heavy Determination 

Test:     00.00% to Key Employees
Plan is/is not Top Heavy

 	Make sure TH % = the actual TH Test %
 	If TH% is 0%, it should be show as 0.00%
 	Make sure check plan is Top Heavy or not (If more than 60%, result should be Plan is Top Heavy & If less than or equals to 60% then Plan is not Top Heavy)

410(b) Coverage Test

Standard:       Pass/Fail Ratio percent 100% - This % denote the result of PS & SHNE contributions

401(k):              Pass/Fail Ratio percent 100% - This % denote the result of SD (Deferrals & Roth) 

401(m):             Pass/Fail Ratio percent 100% - This % denote the result of Match & SH match contributions.

 	If have contributions other than SD/Roth, 410b Test results should be mentioned on the Testing Summary of Results

 	If 410B fails, Testing done with ABPT test. Then Tester had included the wording like below snip
 

Benefits Right and Features Test
Test:    Pass/Fail - This result denotes of BRF test result.

 	Note – we are only adding BRF test result in Result summary, do not include any report regarding BRF test (Result summary only enough)

401(a)(4) Test

Test:    Pass/Fail - This result denotes of 401(a) test result.

414(s)Test

Test:    Pass/Fail - This result denotes of 414(s) test result.



402(g) Deferral Limits

Test:    Pass/Fail - Tester edited the result as per 402g report.


415(c) Annual Additions

Test:    Pass/Fail – Tester edited the result as per the 415 report.


Average Deferral Percentage (ADP)

Test:    Pass/Fail – Tester edited the result as per ADP/ACP test result.

Average Contribution Percentage (ACP)

Test:    Pass/Fail – Tester edited the result as per ADP/ACP test result



