•	You will need to input the QNEC amounts on this CURRENT testing failure notice which will be found on the correction page of the ADP/ACP test.
“ADP/ACP test is $X,XXX,XXX.XX” = the total of both ADP QNEC and the ACP QNEC found on the correction page  (e.g. $142.540.41 + 42,814.34 = $185,354.75)
“ADP QNEC is” = ADP QNEC found on the correction page. (e.g., $142.541.41)
“ACP QNEC is” = ACP QNEC found on the correction page. (e.g., $42,814.34)
(This screen shot shows when both ADP and ACP Test fail)
 
 If only the ADP or ACP Test fails, then the correction page will look like the below screenshot, so you will need to pay attention to what you are reading.
 
 
NOTE: If the ADP/ACP Test is not showing an ADP QNEC or ACP QNEC total then you will remove from the Failure Notice on the one not represented on the ADP/ACP Correction Test Page.
 
NOTE: If the ADP/ACP Test using PRIOR method fails with returns we do NOT include this Failure notice in the Val package.
 
