4. Church Plans
 
This is the UA section needing to be removed from a Church Plan Val Package. 
·UNIVERSAL AVAILABILITY RULE
The “universal availability” generally requires everyone must be able to defer. There is no age or service requirement permitted.  To satisfy universal availability, all employees must have “effective opportunity” to make this deferral election annually At least once during a plan year the plan must provide an employee (whether part-time or full-time) with an effective opportunity to make or change an elective deferral election, up to the dollar limit in effect, including any catch-up deferrals permitted under the plan, as well as Roth contributions if the plan permits. Certain employees may be excluded, including:
·             Employees who normally work less than 20 hours per week*
·             Students performing services at a school, college or university*
·             Non-resident aliens with no U.S. source income
·             Employees who are eligible to make elective deferrals under another 401(k), 403(b) or 457(b) plan sponsored by the same employer
·             Employees not able to defer $200 during the plan year
*For the less than 20 hours per week exclusion and for the student exclusion, if any employee who falls under one of these exclusions has the right to make elective deferrals, then no employee who falls under such exclusions may be prevented from making elective deferrals.
 
This is not part of the UA section.
·If you sponsor a qualified retirement plan not administered by CUNA Mutual Retirement Solutions, please provide your service provider with a copy of this Valuation Report to complete the combined plan testing. Upon request, we can perform the combined plan testing. Please contact your Plan Services Consultant to discuss.
 
457 Assemblies
 
457 Valuation Packages will follow the same general building guidelines as a 401(k) in every aspect. The main difference is that 457 generally only have a 457 Limit Test and a Contribution Analysis and maybe a SOC and/or Failed Excess Returns report. 457 Val Packages are much smaller than other Val Packages.
Manual changes on 457 for “Important Information page:
1.) When a 457 is signed up for Assembly and the tester lets us know that the plan is a 457 Non Governmental, then we need to remove the following paragraphs:
 
 
•	457 Non Governmental Plans do not allow age 50 Catch up contributions.
 
2.) If indicated on the Assembly log, by the tester, that Forfeitures are Reallocated we will keep the following paragraph in the Val, otherwise remove it.
 
 
3.) If indicated on the Assembly Log, by the Tester, that there are no Forfeitures to Reallocate we will keep the following paragraph in the Val, otherwise remove it.
 
4.) If there is no Contribution Analysis report in the Val Package, then we need to remove the following Section from the Val Package:
 
 
