Mid-Year Letter Editing
<Date>
 
For Plan:          <Plan Name>
 
We have completed a mid-year ADP/ACP test for the plan year ending <MM/DD/YYYY>. The information contained in this test is based on the information we currently have on file. Include in all Mid-year letters
 
>The result of this mid-year analysis is attached. It indicates that the maximum actual deferral percentage for all Highly Compensated Employees (HCEs), when averaged together, is within the range allowed. Use this Paragraph when Mid-year is passing
 
>The result of this mid-year analysis is attached. It indicates that the maximum actual deferral percentage for all Highly Compensated Employees (HCEs), when averaged together, exceeds the range allowed. The maximum deferral percentage for the HCEs is <xx.xx%>. Use this paragraph when Mid-year testing is failing.  The HCE Maximum deferral percentage will need to be manually updated from the mid-year test. 
 
>As an alternative to reducing the HCEs deferrals, the employer may contribute enough money to the Non-Highly Compensated Employees by the end of the plan year to satisfy the discrimination test. Use this paragraph, in conjunction with the above failed mid-year paragraph, when Mid-year test is failing and Current method is used
 
Please remember that this is merely a projection based on the current situation. There are many variables that may occur throughout the year that could change this projection. For example, variables could include (but are not limited to): eligible, non-deferring participants entering on the upcoming plan entry date; one or more Highly Compensated Employees terminating employment; and unfavorable market conditions leading to a drop in Non-Highly Compensated Employees participation level. Include in all Mid-year letters
 
Thank you for allowing us to serve you. If you have any questions, please contact your consultant or call us at 844.999.2677. Include in all Mid-year letters
 
CUNA Mutual Retirement Solutions Include in all Mid-year letters
 
